      "title": "M2.6 · Descriptor",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "M2.6: the Descriptor type (M5_DESCRIPTOR).\n\nThe input is m5_melody.desc.json (copied into input/ by the workflow runner; otherwise copy it from custom_nodes/com5fy/workflows/inputs/). It's a hand-made analysis of 3 s of a four-note melody (A3, C4, E4, then a G4 30 cents flat), 50 ms hop: f0 (Hz, with vibrato, missing in the last 100 ms), loudness (dB), onsets (4 times), and partials (a frame matrix: index, frequency, amplitude; 3 harmonics per note).\n\nPress Run. Look at:\n1. Loaded descriptor (Preview as Text): one line per track with points/frames, time span, range and unit. (The real Descriptor viewer, with a table and plots, is M3.5.)\n2. Sequence Viewer: two staves. \"onsets\": one note per onset, lasting until the next one, pitched at the median f0 over that span: A3 C4 E4 G4, the G4 with a -29 cents label. \"partials\": 12 notes, the 3 harmonics of each note (A3 A4 E5 +2 cents, ...), one note per partial index.\n3. f0 as a BPF, shown read-only (green) in a BPF node: 58 points (the 2 missing f0 frames are skipped), exp, unit Hz, range 50-2000. \"Edit a copy\" turns it into a drawable curve.\n\nTry: clear \"partials\" or \"pitch\" in Descriptor to Sequence (blank = not used); raise min_partial_ms above 650 to drop the G4's partials; name \"loudness\" in Descriptor to BPF. A name the descriptor doesn't have gives an error listing the names it does have.\nYour own files: put a .json or .csv in input/ and press R. CSV: time_ms (or time_s) column, then one column per series, e.g. \"f0 [Hz]\"."
      ],
